{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-neutron-prediction-comparison","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:neutron-prediction-comparison","kind":"proposition","title":"Comparison of predicted and observed stable neutron numbers for $p \\leq 103$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-integer-stability"],"tags":["stability-cubic","neutron-number","codata","comparison","beta-stability"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.stable_neutron_max_error","text":"neutron-prediction-comparison.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/neutron-prediction-comparison.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:neutron-prediction-comparison\"></a><p>At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = q_0</code>, the beta-stability formula (<a href=\"#prop:beta-stability\">beta-stability</a>) predicts a stable neutron number <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_{\\mathrm{pred}}(p)</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  p^*(A) =  \\frac{A}{2 + c \\cdot A^{2/3}},\n  \\qquad c = \\frac{a_C}{2a_A} = 0.01497.</code></pre>\n<p>We compare this against observed isotopes across 103 elements:</p>\n<p>See <a href=\"#tbl:neutron-prediction-comparison-table-data\">Table</a>.</p>\n<p>The mean discrepancy is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\overline{|\\Delta n|} = 1.7</code>. The maximum discrepancy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">|\\Delta n| = 8</code> occurs at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p = 102</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p = 103</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/neutron-prediction-comparison.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"16.5.2"}
